WEBVTT

1
00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:10.989
The children introduced themselves to the boy.

2
00:00:10.990 --> 00:00:13.687
"I'm Will," he said.

3
00:00:13.688 --> 00:00:16.877
"I'm going to my father's workshop."

4
00:00:16.878 --> 00:00:20.513
"Workshop?" asked Mandy.

5
00:00:20.514 --> 00:00:23.830
"He's a cooper," said Will.

6
00:00:23.831 --> 00:00:26.510
"I help him build barrels.

7
00:00:26.511 --> 00:00:29.213
What does your father do?"

8
00:00:29.214 --> 00:00:34.314
"Well, right now he's building a den," said Vinnie.

9
00:00:34.315 --> 00:00:38.957
"A den?" asked Will, confused.

10
00:00:38.958 --> 00:00:44.619
"Forget it, Will. Vinnie's just joking," said Mandy.

11
00:00:44.620 --> 00:00:50.056
The grocer had stepped down, and the crowd was breaking up.

12
00:00:50.057 --> 00:00:54.917
"Well, the speech is over," said Vinnie.

13
00:00:54.918 --> 00:00:59.707
"Will, we need your help," said Mandy.

14
00:00:59.708 --> 00:01:02.975
"We must find John Adams."

15
00:01:02.976 --> 00:01:06.956
Will stopped smiling and stared at them.

16
00:01:06.957 --> 00:01:11.632
"Who sent you?" he asked suspiciously.

17
00:01:11.633 --> 00:01:15.387
Vinnie explained what happened on the docks.

18
00:01:15.388 --> 00:01:19.278
"You must see my father," said Will.

19
00:01:19.279 --> 00:01:22.208
"He knows where Mr. Adams is."

20
00:01:22.209 --> 00:01:27.016
Vinnie and Mandy walked to Will's father's workshop.

21
00:01:27.017 --> 00:01:31.427
It was in a large house where Will's family lived.

22
00:01:31.428 --> 00:01:35.860
Strips of wood were stacked high outside the shop.

23
00:01:35.861 --> 00:01:40.273
Inside, a man was sitting on a bench.

24
00:01:40.274 --> 00:01:45.630
He was scraping a strip of wood with a two-handled knife.

25
00:01:45.631 --> 00:01:49.487
"What's he doing?" asked Mandy.

26
00:01:49.488 --> 00:01:51.484
"That's my dad.

27
00:01:51.485 --> 00:01:56.808
He's shaping a strip of wood to fit a barrel," Will explained.

28
00:01:56.809 --> 00:02:03.192
"Next he'll arrange all the strips inside metal hoops that will hold them together."

29
00:02:03.193 --> 00:02:09.712
"Will! Are you ready to help your tired father?" laughed the man.

30
00:02:09.713 --> 00:02:14.467
"These are my new friends, Vinnie and Mandy," said Will.

31
00:02:14.468 --> 00:02:18.530
"Hello, children!" cried Will's father.

32
00:02:18.531 --> 00:02:22.020
"Welcome to our home and shop."

33
00:02:22.021 --> 00:02:27.843
"Father, Vinnie and Mandy have a special message for Mr. Adams," said Will.

34
00:02:27.844 --> 00:02:32.703
Suddenly serious, his father looked at the children.

35
00:02:32.704 --> 00:02:36.047
"Let me see it," he said.

36
00:02:36.048 --> 00:02:38.642
Vinnie shook his head.

37
00:02:38.643 --> 00:02:43.614
"I'm sorry, sir, but only Mr. Adams can see it."

38
00:02:43.615 --> 00:02:47.100
Mandy looked at Vinnie proudly.

39
00:02:47.101 --> 00:02:51.566
He was taking his responsibility seriously.

40
00:02:51.567 --> 00:02:56.541
"Will, take the children inside," said his father.

41
00:02:56.542 --> 00:02:59.774
"Then go to the silversmith and find Mr. Revere.

42
00:02:59.775 --> 00:03:01.692
He will help."

43
00:03:01.693 --> 00:03:06.602
Will led Vinnie and Mandy through the house to a warm kitchen.

44
00:03:06.603 --> 00:03:12.521
In a large fireplace, a black pot was bubbling.

45
00:03:12.522 --> 00:03:18.208
The children saw more pots and pans hanging above the fireplace.

46
00:03:18.209 --> 00:03:24.674
Two little girls sat on the floor playing with cloth dolls and little teacups.

47
00:03:24.675 --> 00:03:30.274
"These are my twin sisters, Margaret and Jane," said Will.

48
00:03:30.275 --> 00:03:34.613
"Who are your friends, Will?" asked Will's mother.

49
00:03:34.614 --> 00:03:38.597
She sat at a table peeling potatoes.

50
00:03:38.598 --> 00:03:44.744
Will introduced Mandy and Vinnie, and then Mandy spoke to the girls.

51
00:03:44.745 --> 00:03:49.106
"What are your dolls doing?" she asked.

52
00:03:49.107 --> 00:03:54.294
"They are having a tea party," explained Margaret.

53
00:03:54.295 --> 00:03:59.180
"But this tea is not from England," said Jane.

54
00:03:59.181 --> 00:04:03.931
"British tea is very bad," said Margaret.

55
00:04:03.932 --> 00:04:10.765
"Didn't John Hancock get arrested for smuggling tea?" Vinnie whispered to Mandy.

56
00:04:10.766 --> 00:04:13.489
Will interrupted them.

57
00:04:13.490 --> 00:04:17.595
"Stay here. I will be right back," he said.

58
00:04:17.596 --> 00:04:21.837
"My mother will look after you."

59
00:04:21.838 --> 00:04:24.028
"Would you like some tea?"

60
00:04:24.029 --> 00:04:33.113
asked Jane, holding up a tiny teacup.
